WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.550
Welcome.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.781
In this video, I'll show you exactly

00:00:03.781 --> 00:00:06.010
how to use your Day-1 Setup Kit.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.196
It's the checklist that takes you from

00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:10.382
knowing nothing about crypto to set up

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:12.420
safely, and ready for Module 1.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.319
We'll go through it part by part,

00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:16.163
with what to do, why it matters,

00:00:16.163 --> 00:00:17.615
and the mistakes to avoid.

00:00:18.915 --> 00:00:20.135
Here's the kit.

00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:22.962
It's a short printable PDF, four pages, in

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:25.695
the Start here section of the course.

00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:28.133
It holds a setup roadmap, a checklist

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.186
in six parts, ten rules to keep

00:00:30.186 --> 00:00:32.795
forever, and two reference diagrams.

00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:35.110
Download it, and if you can, print it.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.955
Ticking boxes on paper, with a

00:00:36.955 --> 00:00:38.502
pen, is part of the point.

00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:42.177
Before you start, gather what you'll need.

00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:45.749
Photo ID for the exchange's identity checks.

00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:47.004
A bank account.

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:49.464
A smartphone for an authenticator app.

00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:51.854
A computer with an up-to-date browser.

00:00:51.854 --> 00:00:53.327
Pen and paper, or a metal

00:00:53.327 --> 00:00:55.610
backup plate, for your seed phrase.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.543
And, optionally, a hardware wallet

00:00:57.543 --> 00:00:59.555
bought directly from the maker.

00:00:59.555 --> 00:01:01.583
Plan on 2 to 3 hours in total,

00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.722
spread over a few days, because identity checks

00:01:04.722 --> 00:01:06.815
and bank deposits can take time.

00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:10.410
Four ground rules for using the kit.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.233
Go in order, because every part

00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:14.015
depends on the one before.

00:01:14.015 --> 00:01:16.110
Use a small learning amount only, money

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.190
you could lose without it hurting.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.080
Tick each box only when it's truly

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.000
done, not when you've read it.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.712
And write things down as you go,

00:01:23.712 --> 00:01:25.735
because your records sheet starts here.

00:01:27.035 --> 00:01:29.330
Here's the whole journey on one page.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.340
Accounts.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.435
Exchange.

00:01:31.435 --> 00:01:32.590
First buy.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.530
Wallet.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.865
First transfer.

00:01:34.865 --> 00:01:36.230
Practice DeFi.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.005
And a security baseline.

00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:40.688
The checklist follows exactly this order,

00:01:40.688 --> 00:01:42.330
in six parts, A to F.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.725
Let's go through each one.

00:01:45.025 --> 00:01:46.590
Part A is accounts, and

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.585
it takes about 45 minutes.

00:01:48.585 --> 00:01:50.913
Start with a password manager, and write

00:01:50.913 --> 00:01:53.485
its master password down somewhere safe.

00:01:53.485 --> 00:01:55.890
Secure your email with a unique password

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.530
and an authenticator app, because your email

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.825
is the key to every other account.

00:02:00.825 --> 00:02:04.154
Then choose an exchange that's legally available where

00:02:04.154 --> 00:02:06.696
you live and has a solid reputation, open

00:02:06.696 --> 00:02:09.540
your account, and complete the identity checks.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.110
Before you deposit a cent, lock the exchange down.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:17.234
Turn on two-factor with an authenticator app or a

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:20.970
security key, not text messages, which can be hijacked.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.040
Store the backup codes offline.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.036
Switch on the anti-phishing code, so every real

00:02:26.036 --> 00:02:29.270
email from the exchange shows your secret word.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.005
And switch on the withdrawal allowlist, so money

00:02:32.005 --> 00:02:34.740
can only ever leave to addresses you've approved.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.320
Part B is your first purchase, about 20 minutes.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.566
Deposit a small learning amount, using

00:02:41.566 --> 00:02:44.228
the cheapest method your exchange offers.

00:02:44.228 --> 00:02:46.708
Buy a little ETH, which you'll need

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.188
to pay network fees, and some USDC,

00:02:49.188 --> 00:02:52.313
a dollar stablecoin you'll practise with.

00:02:52.313 --> 00:02:54.092
Then try one limit order, so you

00:02:54.092 --> 00:02:56.032
learn to set your own price instead

00:02:56.032 --> 00:02:58.188
of taking whatever the market gives you.

00:02:59.488 --> 00:03:01.433
Here's why the method matters.

00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:02.693
The price on the chart

00:03:02.693 --> 00:03:04.088
is not what you pay.

00:03:04.088 --> 00:03:05.818
You lose a little to the spread, a

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.795
little to the trading fee, and a little

00:03:07.795 --> 00:03:09.973
more to the network when you withdraw.

00:03:09.973 --> 00:03:11.922
Compare what actually lands in your

00:03:11.922 --> 00:03:13.600
wallet, not the headline price.

00:03:14.899 --> 00:03:16.601
The last box in Part B is your

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:19.482
records sheet, and it's simpler than it sounds.

00:03:19.482 --> 00:03:21.317
One row for every action.

00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:22.342
The date.

00:03:22.342 --> 00:03:23.437
What you did.

00:03:23.437 --> 00:03:24.527
The amount.

00:03:24.527 --> 00:03:25.587
The price.

00:03:25.587 --> 00:03:26.777
And the fees.

00:03:26.777 --> 00:03:30.632
Here's an example row for a small ETH purchase.

00:03:30.632 --> 00:03:32.423
Keep it from day one, and tax

00:03:32.423 --> 00:03:34.812
time, and your own reviews, become easy.

00:03:36.112 --> 00:03:38.922
Part C is your wallet, about 30 minutes.

00:03:38.922 --> 00:03:41.627
Install it only from the official website,

00:03:41.627 --> 00:03:44.332
ideally in a separate browser profile that

00:03:44.332 --> 00:03:46.142
you use just for crypto.

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.703
When it shows you a new seed phrase, write

00:03:48.703 --> 00:03:51.207
it down, on paper or metal, in order.

00:03:51.207 --> 00:03:53.881
Never type it into a computer, never photograph

00:03:53.881 --> 00:03:55.887
it, and never store it in the cloud.

00:03:57.187 --> 00:03:59.082
The seed phrase is your wallet.

00:03:59.082 --> 00:04:01.515
Anyone who has it owns your funds, and if

00:04:01.515 --> 00:04:04.422
you lose it, nobody can recover them for you.

00:04:04.422 --> 00:04:06.257
Here are the dos and don'ts.

00:04:06.257 --> 00:04:08.225
Write it on paper or stamp it in

00:04:08.225 --> 00:04:10.729
metal, in order, keep it private and safe

00:04:10.729 --> 00:04:13.054
from fire and water, and keep a second

00:04:13.054 --> 00:04:15.560
copy elsewhere once the amount grows.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.461
Never photograph it or keep it in notes, email

00:04:18.461 --> 00:04:21.177
or the cloud, never share it, and never use

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:24.387
a phrase that came pre-printed or from someone else.

00:04:25.687 --> 00:04:27.442
Then do the restore test.

00:04:27.442 --> 00:04:29.027
It's the most skipped box in

00:04:29.027 --> 00:04:31.077
the kit, and the most important.

00:04:31.077 --> 00:04:33.913
Before you put money in, note your wallet address.

00:04:33.913 --> 00:04:35.808
Remove the wallet from the app.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.123
Restore it from your written seed phrase.

00:04:38.123 --> 00:04:40.528
Then check that the same address appears.

00:04:40.528 --> 00:04:42.433
If it does, your backup works.

00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:43.886
If it doesn't, you found out

00:04:43.886 --> 00:04:45.538
while the wallet was empty.

00:04:45.538 --> 00:04:48.650
Finally, save the wallet's address, the address only,

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.013
never the seed, in your password manager.

00:04:52.313 --> 00:04:55.653
Part D is your first transfer, about 20 minutes.

00:04:55.653 --> 00:04:57.600
Choose a low-fee network that both

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.013
your exchange and your wallet support.

00:05:00.013 --> 00:05:03.391
Then send a small test first, for example

00:05:03.391 --> 00:05:06.748
$10 of ETH, and wait until it arrives.

00:05:06.748 --> 00:05:09.279
Only then send the rest of your learning funds,

00:05:09.279 --> 00:05:12.531
and add your wallet's address to the exchange allowlist.

00:05:12.531 --> 00:05:15.201
Finally, find the transfer on a block explorer,

00:05:15.201 --> 00:05:16.926
so you can see it for yourself.

00:05:18.226 --> 00:05:20.381
Here's the transfer step by step.

00:05:20.381 --> 00:05:22.741
The network you choose at the exchange must

00:05:22.741 --> 00:05:24.971
match the network your wallet is on.

00:05:24.971 --> 00:05:27.266
Copy the address with the wallet's copy

00:05:27.266 --> 00:05:29.332
button, never type it, and check at

00:05:29.332 --> 00:05:31.927
least the first and last six characters.

00:05:31.927 --> 00:05:33.402
Send the small test.

00:05:33.402 --> 00:05:35.107
Wait until it arrives.

00:05:35.107 --> 00:05:37.237
Then send the rest, and keep a

00:05:37.237 --> 00:05:39.942
little ETH on that network for gas.

00:05:39.942 --> 00:05:42.097
The test costs one extra small fee,

00:05:42.097 --> 00:05:44.133
and it protects you from the most

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:46.827
common, and most permanent, beginner mistake.

00:05:48.127 --> 00:05:50.937
Part E is practice, about 30 minutes.

00:05:50.937 --> 00:05:53.940
Add the Sepolia test network to your wallet,

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.642
and get free test ETH from a faucet.

00:05:56.642 --> 00:05:59.070
Make one practice transaction there, where

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.782
nothing real is at stake.

00:06:00.782 --> 00:06:02.717
Then make one tiny real swap on

00:06:02.717 --> 00:06:05.617
a low-fee network, with a limited approval.

00:06:05.617 --> 00:06:07.752
And afterwards, revoke that approval.

00:06:09.052 --> 00:06:10.687
The order is the lesson.

00:06:10.687 --> 00:06:13.562
Test network first, with free test tokens.

00:06:13.562 --> 00:06:15.732
Connect only from a bookmarked site.

00:06:15.732 --> 00:06:17.624
Read what the wallet asks you to

00:06:17.624 --> 00:06:19.644
sign: what, to whom, how much.

00:06:19.644 --> 00:06:21.534
And the tiny real amount comes

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:23.484
last, only after the test works.

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:27.019
Here's why the last box matters.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.212
When an app asks to move your tokens,

00:06:29.212 --> 00:06:31.809
it's asking for an approval, and an approval

00:06:31.809 --> 00:06:34.129
stays open after the trade is done.

00:06:34.129 --> 00:06:35.650
Give an exact amount, not

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:38.056
unlimited, and revoke it afterwards.

00:06:38.056 --> 00:06:40.482
You'll learn to read approvals properly in

00:06:40.482 --> 00:06:42.626
Module 1, but this habit starts today.

00:06:43.925 --> 00:06:47.591
Part F is your security baseline, about 15 minutes.

00:06:47.591 --> 00:06:49.074
Read the ten rules, and make

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:50.856
sure you understand each one.

00:06:50.856 --> 00:06:53.169
Bookmark the sites you use, and never

00:06:53.169 --> 00:06:55.416
reach them from ads or messages.

00:06:55.416 --> 00:06:57.476
Order a hardware wallet from the maker,

00:06:57.476 --> 00:06:59.681
for when the amount starts to matter.

00:06:59.681 --> 00:07:01.616
And bring your records sheet up to date.

00:07:02.916 --> 00:07:04.571
Here are the ten rules, the part

00:07:04.571 --> 00:07:06.426
of the kit you'll keep forever.

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:07.246
One.

00:07:07.246 --> 00:07:09.996
Never share your seed phrase; no real person

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:12.251
or company will ever ask for it.

00:07:12.251 --> 00:07:13.121
Two.

00:07:13.121 --> 00:07:15.470
Bookmark the sites you use, and never

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:18.242
reach them from ads, messages or emails.

00:07:18.242 --> 00:07:19.152
Three.

00:07:19.152 --> 00:07:21.572
Nobody legitimate messages you first

00:07:21.572 --> 00:07:24.422
offering help, investments or recovery.

00:07:24.422 --> 00:07:25.307
Four.

00:07:25.307 --> 00:07:27.972
Guaranteed returns are a scam, always.

00:07:27.972 --> 00:07:28.912
Five.

00:07:28.912 --> 00:07:31.398
Read every wallet prompt before approving:

00:07:31.398 --> 00:07:33.017
what, how much, and to whom.

00:07:34.317 --> 00:07:35.237
Six.

00:07:35.237 --> 00:07:38.297
Test first, with a small amount, on anything new.

00:07:38.297 --> 00:07:39.202
Seven.

00:07:39.202 --> 00:07:40.631
Use a hardware wallet once

00:07:40.631 --> 00:07:42.307
the amount matters to you.

00:07:42.307 --> 00:07:43.172
Eight.

00:07:43.172 --> 00:07:45.310
Keep your devices updated, and use

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.932
a separate browser profile for crypto.

00:07:47.932 --> 00:07:48.822
Nine.

00:07:48.822 --> 00:07:52.262
Keep records of every buy, sell, transfer and fee.

00:07:52.262 --> 00:07:53.277
And ten.

00:07:53.277 --> 00:07:55.502
If something feels urgent, stop.

00:07:55.502 --> 00:07:57.392
Scammers create urgency.

00:07:57.392 --> 00:07:58.787
Real opportunities wait.

00:08:00.087 --> 00:08:01.835
These rules exist because the

00:08:01.835 --> 00:08:03.882
same attacks happen every day.

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:07.027
Fake websites that look exactly like the real one.

00:08:07.027 --> 00:08:10.227
Drainers that empty a wallet with a single signature.

00:08:10.227 --> 00:08:13.252
Fake support staff who ask for your seed phrase.

00:08:13.252 --> 00:08:16.152
And poisoned addresses planted in your history.

00:08:16.152 --> 00:08:18.567
The ten rules close every one of these doors.

00:08:19.867 --> 00:08:22.192
Here are the mistakes we see most often.

00:08:22.192 --> 00:08:23.937
Skipping the restore test.

00:08:23.937 --> 00:08:27.247
Choosing text-message two-factor because it's easier.

00:08:27.247 --> 00:08:28.862
Sending on the wrong network,

00:08:28.862 --> 00:08:30.777
or skipping the test transfer.

00:08:30.777 --> 00:08:32.398
Storing the seed phrase in a

00:08:32.398 --> 00:08:33.872
notes app or a photo.

00:08:33.872 --> 00:08:36.122
And rushing to finish in one sitting.

00:08:36.122 --> 00:08:37.577
Take the few days.

00:08:37.577 --> 00:08:38.412
It's worth it.

00:08:39.712 --> 00:08:40.997
If you get stuck.

00:08:40.997 --> 00:08:43.583
Identity checks and bank deposits can take

00:08:43.583 --> 00:08:45.507
a day or two; that's normal, so

00:08:45.507 --> 00:08:47.792
move on to reading and come back.

00:08:47.792 --> 00:08:50.153
If a transfer hasn't arrived, find it on

00:08:50.153 --> 00:08:53.102
the block explorer before doing anything else.

00:08:53.102 --> 00:08:54.977
And if anyone messages you offering

00:08:54.977 --> 00:08:56.632
to help, that's a scammer.

00:08:56.632 --> 00:08:59.012
Our support will never message you first,

00:08:59.012 --> 00:09:01.052
and never asks for your seed phrase.

00:09:02.352 --> 00:09:04.027
Let's check two things.

00:09:04.027 --> 00:09:05.237
Question one.

00:09:05.237 --> 00:09:06.470
Why do you send a small

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.012
test before the full transfer?

00:09:12.432 --> 00:09:14.501
The answer: to prove the network and

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:16.793
address are right, while a mistake would

00:09:16.793 --> 00:09:18.247
only cost the test amount.

00:09:19.547 --> 00:09:20.792
Question two.

00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:22.277
When is Part C really done?

00:09:26.697 --> 00:09:29.276
The answer: when the restore test has passed,

00:09:29.276 --> 00:09:31.743
and the same address appears, not just when

00:09:31.743 --> 00:09:33.537
the seed phrase is written down.

00:09:34.837 --> 00:09:37.012
When every box is ticked, you're done.

00:09:37.012 --> 00:09:39.839
Your accounts are secured, your wallet is backed

00:09:39.839 --> 00:09:42.320
up and proven, you've made a real transfer

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.167
and a real swap, and you have a

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:46.717
security baseline you'll keep for life.

00:09:46.717 --> 00:09:49.882
You're ready for Module 1: Foundations and Safety.

00:09:51.182 --> 00:09:52.979
Download the kit, print it, and

00:09:52.979 --> 00:09:54.627
start with Part A today.

00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:55.887
Take your time.

00:09:55.887 --> 00:09:57.352
I'll see you in Module 1.
